  "conclusion": "The exact host posting code accepts locally valid but unequal payload lengths, advances all sequence flags, and leaves a previous two-slot payload tail intact. Native sanitizers report no fault because all reads/writes remain in initialized allocated memory. This is a demonstrated mechanism, not a capture of production tail contents.",
  "limitations": [
    "Host Apple arm64 execution, not Linux HCA/NIC/GPU execution; Linux-only thread placement path is not run.",
    "Unchanged simulator substitutes fake verbs and GPU endpoints; it does not qualify NIC coherence, GPU memory ordering, actual memory registration or generated GPU instructions.",
    "Narrow payload test calls actual post_op and fake FIFO delivery without proxy threads or doorbell publication; the unchanged simulator separately exercises proxy threads and missed doorbells.",
    "Narrow controls reuse slot1 at sequences1 and3 with actual17x5120 BF16 payload sizes; all-ones and finite prior payloads are specified controls, not captured production bytes.",
    "The source of production rank-count divergence and the first actual NaN-producing operation require contemporaneous runtime evidence. Other kernel defects are not excluded."
